   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to making available information regarding the process for\nindividuals to obtain eligibility for services offered by the office for\npeople with developmental disabilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S5347",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5347-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 7,
       "fullName": "Anna Kaplan",
       "imgName": "1044_Anna_Kaplan.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1224,
       "sessionMemberId": 1222,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "KAPLAN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Social Services",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5347\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to making available information\nregarding the process for individuals to obtain eligibility for services\noffered by the office for people with developmental disabilities\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo make available on the office website information on services offered\nby the OPWDD and to establish a better understanding of the service\ndelivery process effected individuals and their families can take to\nobtain eligibility and receive such services.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 requires OPWDD to post on its website information regarding\nthe process for individuals to obtain eligibility for services\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Office for People with Developmental Disabilities (OPWDD) is a\nlarge, complex agency that provides services to thousands of people. It\nis often difficult for people seeking services and their families to\nnavigate the system. This bill would require OPWDD to make information\navailable relating to the Front Door Process,\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
